<Article title="Privacy">
  <p>
    Motile is built so that your work stays on your own machines. This page says
    what the service at motile.app stores and what it never sees.
  </p>

  <h2>What we store</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Your Google account's basics:</strong> its identifier, your email
      address, your name and your profile picture, as Google gives them to us
      when you sign in.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your devices:</strong> for each client and each server you link, its
      public key, the name you see for it, its platform and when it was linked.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Short-lived sign-in and install codes:</strong> stored as hashes
      and deleted when they expire, within an hour.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your sessions on the web:</strong> signing in at app.motile.app
      opens a session that lasts 30 days. We store its hash, and your browser
      keeps it in one cookie. We set no other cookies.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we never see</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Your threads, prompts, code and files.</strong> They live on your
      servers and in the client on your devices. The client connects straight to your
      server, encrypted end to end with the devices' keys.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your agents' sign-ins.</strong> Claude Code and Codex are signed
      in on your servers, not with us.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    When a client and a server can't reach each other directly, their traffic passes
    through one of iroh's public relays. It stays encrypted between the two
    devices; the relay can't read it.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <p>
    Only to sign you in and to tell your servers which clients are yours. We don't
    sell it, share it or use it for advertising.
  </p>

  <h2>Deleting it</h2>
  <p>
    Signing out of a client removes that client from your account, and you can remove
    any client or server at <a href="https://app.motile.app" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">app.motile.app</a>. To
    delete your account, write to{" "}
    <a href="mailto:privacy@motile.app">privacy@motile.app</a>.
  </p>
</Article>
